cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "paperlint: deterministic pre-submission gates for manuscripts and research repositories"
abstract: >
  A command-line tool that verifies published claims about research artefacts:
  page counts, recorded hashes and byte sizes, citation/bibliography parity,
  figure rendering determinism, Word template structure, CI workflow wiring and
  deposit records. Every check is independent and the exit code is the contract,
  so the tool can gate a submission pipeline. A run that executes zero checks
  exits non-zero.
type: software
